   "id": "pesachim.74a.6",
   "daf": "74a",
   "sentenceId": 5,
   "he": "וְנוֹתֵן אֶת כְּרָעָיו וְכוּ׳. תַּנְיָא: רַבִּי יִשְׁמָעֵאל קוֹרֵיהוּ ״תּוֹךְ תּוֹךְ״. רַבִּי טַרְפוֹן קוֹרֵיהוּ ״גְּדִי מְקוּלָּס״.",
   "en": "It was taught in the mishna that according to the opinion of Rabbi Yosei HaGelili, «one places the legs» and entrails inside the lamb’s body and roasts them together. «It was taught» in a baraita: «Rabbi Yishmael» would «call» the Paschal lamb: «Tokh, tokh,» because when one roasts the legs and entrails inside the lamb they make that sound, like other things that are cooked. «Rabbi Tarfon» would «call it: Helmeted kid.» In his opinion, the entrails must be roasted when they are suspended from the spit above the head of the animal, somewhat resembling a helmet."
  }
 ],
